sentences.l:
Neither by winds is it shaken, nor ever with rain
is it wetted, nor does snow come near, but very clear sky
is spread cloudless, and white radiance has run over it;

and at once she marvelled at the dream,
and set out to go through the halls, that she might tell her parents,
her dear father and mother;

sentences.t:
πάππα φίλ’, οὐκ ἂν δή μοι ἐφοπλίσσειας ἀπήνην
ὑψηλὴν ἐύκυκλον, ἵνα κλυτὰ εἵματ’ ἄγωμαι
ἐς ποταμὸν πλυνέουσα, τά μοι ῥερυπωμένα κεῖται;

sentences.l:
As Artemis, arrow-pourer, goes over the mountains,
either along Taygetus, very long, or Erymanthus,
taking delight in boars and swift deer;
